1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,800
At 9:12, Invoice 447 lands in an agent's queue.
Value: $84,600. Mismatch: 6.2%.

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:15,460
The instruction is simple:
“Resolve material discrepancies with the appropriate approver.”

3
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:20,920
Accounts Payable says, “Hold it.”
Procurement says, “Protect supply.” Operations says, “Pay now.”

4
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:26,560
Correct it later. Three reasonable answers.
One agent waiting for a rule.

5
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:32,200
It cannot decide whose priority wins, what “material” means,
or who approves an exception.

6
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:40,680
Humans bridge ambiguity through experience and informal conversations.
The agent makes the invisible operating model visible.

7
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:51,640
Before asking whether the agent can reason, ask whether the organization
can explain the work: outcome, owner, decision right, exception path, and success measure.

8
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:58,680
The first agent-readiness test is surprisingly human:
can two experienced people explain the same decision in the same way?
